WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.367
Russian

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:01.034
President Vladimir

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.836
Putin says his country will now station

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.404
tactical nuclear weapons

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.106
right on NATO's doorstep.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.474
Today, Putin announced an agreement

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.375
with Belarus

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.710
and says a special storage facility

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.212
for those weapons will be built there

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.380
by July.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.216
As you can see, Belarus borders both

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.085
naito ally Poland and Ukraine and CNN.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.787
A former CNN Moscow bureau

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.255
chief, Jill Dougherty, joins us now.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.423
She's an adjunct professor

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.859
at Georgetown University.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.660
Jill, I mean, we've we've heard

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.361
Vladimir Putin

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.329
try so many times

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:31.831
to be provocative when it comes to,

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:32.932
you know,

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.335
injecting the prospect of nuclear weapons

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.437
into this war in Ukraine.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.938
Your reaction to this announcement?

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.640
Is it just more of that bluster?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.743
Should it be taken more seriously?

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.312
I think what he's trying to do,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.182
as usual, is raise the threat level.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.817
And as soon as you use

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:51.484
the word

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.119
nuclear, regardless

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:56.022
what kind of nukes he's talking about

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.224
is frightening and it gets attention.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:00:59.759
And I know saying that

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.061
we should diminish it, Jim,

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:01.561
that I think,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.062
you know,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.396
as usual with President

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.498
Putin, you have to read the fine print

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.367
and put it into context.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.902
So what he's saying is

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.602
you said

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.805
that we will station these

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.606
tactical nuclear weapons,

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.876
you know, field weapons in Belarus.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.978
And the question is, you know,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.314
when will this happen? Maybe this summer.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.550
But I think the important thing is he's

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.651
not saying

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.385
and in fact, he's

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.020
saying they will not put them

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.789
in the hands of Alexander Lukashenko,

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.058
who is the president of Belarus.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.960
And that could be a problem.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.395
He is keeping control,

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.531
he says, in the hands of himself,

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.067
obviously, and in Russia in general.

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:43.403
So I do think that

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.505
in all of these things,

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.140
as soon as you kind of begin

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.241
upping the ante

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:48.875
when you're talking

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.243
about nuclear weapons,

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.745
provocative, sometimes dangerous

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.648
But I do not think that,

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.516
you know, it's

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.651
panic time or anything like that.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.686
It's Putin

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.154
trying to escalate

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.589
because he has problems

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:04.491
right.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.926
I mean, we've seen that time and again

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:07.527
in Ukraine.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.696
And do you think this decision

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.731
will force any sort of countermove

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.632
by the U.S.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.900
or naito,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.169
or do they just keep an eye on it

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:16.936
and see,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:17.303
you know,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.305
how much he really does deliver on this?

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.742
Well, don't forget that the United States

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:25.111
itself has tactical nuclear weapons

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.279
in Europe.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.113
In fact,

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:27.847
Putin mentioned

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.517
there are six bases where they are kept

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:33.353
and that actually apparently is correct,

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.854
that there are six bases

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:35.922
where the United States

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.857
keeps weapons like that.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.159
But they are really under

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.493
control of the U.S.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.996
Air Force and they are on bases.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.164
There are not just spread

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.331
all over the place.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.833
So is Putin saying

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.101
and very much

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.403
we've seen this, Jim, in the Ukraine war,

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:53.006
you're doing something It's our turn.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.041
We're going to do it.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.709
But again, it you know,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.178
it does upped the ante.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:58.811
And if you have

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.613
more nuclear weapons there,

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.315
and then also I think it raises

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.483
a real question,

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.852
what why is Lukashenko

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.520
even agreeing to this?

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:07.820
You know,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.889
this is something he gave up

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.057
nuclear weapons.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.392
Ukraine Belarus,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.159
they all gave him up

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.694
back in the early nineties.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.696
Why does he want any type

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.298
of nuclear weapon back?

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.133
Right.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:20.700
I mean,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.401
and Joe, I

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.435
was just about to ask you that.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.970
I mean, Belarus

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.838
has had no nuclear weapons

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.875
in its territory since the early 1990s.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:32.812
That I mean, that of itself does

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.781
present an escalation.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:35.448
I mean,

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.617
whether you want to call this a Cold War

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:38.351
between the U.S.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.287
and Russia, I mean it is it's provocative

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.390
it's provocative.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.325
And it's also is

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.759
I think, a sign of weakness,

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:47.293
you know,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.561
weakness by Putin

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.463
because one of the only things

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.297
that he can do right

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.366
now, let's, let's look at a situation

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.401
He did not get a whole lot

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.369
out of that meeting

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.338
with the Chinese president Xi.

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:01.808
He is now the ICC has issued a warrant

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:04.077
for his arrest as a war criminal.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.912
And then also the fighting in Ukraine

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.480
isn't going very well.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.782
So the one thing that Vladimir Putin has

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.918
all the time in his pocket

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.886
is his nuclear weapons.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.922
So he tends to

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.925
resort to bluster about those threats.

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.994
And I think that's what we've got here.

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.662
But every time you do that,

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.030
it does get more dangerous

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.933
because there will be apparently new

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.068
tactical weapons in Belarus.

